@page {
    meta: {
        title: "Rocdown language reference",
        description: "Look up Rocdown page metadata, declarations, Markdown behavior, links, themes, routes, and generated values.",
    },
}

# Rocdown language reference

Rocdown is Markdown with explicit document-root declarations. Ordinary prose,
email addresses, handles, and fenced code retain their Markdown meaning.

## Declaration recognition

A reserved declaration is recognized only when it starts at the document root,
after optional indentation, and its header matches the expected shape. Reserved
names inside lists, block quotes, or fences stay Markdown.

Use `\@roc` for a literal line-start declaration example outside a fence.

## Declarations

| Form | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `@page { ... }` | Route, draft, layout, theme, color scheme, and metadata |
| `@roc { ... }` | Roc imports, types, and values |
| `@render { expr }` | Insert one Roc `Html` expression |
| `@component` | Declare a Rocci component |
| `@fixture` | Tag preview or test data |
| `@css { ... }` | Add file-scoped CSS |
| `@context`, `@init`, `@on` | Declare a standalone server app |
| `@if`, `@for`, `@match`, `@let` | Insert document-root Rocci template regions |
| `<Tag />` | Instantiate a document-root Rocci component or element |

`@island` is reserved in the design but not parsed yet.

## Page metadata

````rocdown
@page {
    route: "/guides/rocdown/",
    draft: Bool.false,
    theme: "paper",
    color_scheme: "auto",
    meta: {
        title: "Rocdown",
        description: "Markdown with explicit Roc and Rocci regions",
    },
}
````

| Field | Constraint |
| --- | --- |
| `route` | Absolute string path; no `..`, query, fragment, encoded separator, or NUL |
| `layout` | Statically resolvable Roc value path |
| `draft` | `Bool.true` or `Bool.false` |
| `theme` | Built-in ID, local theme ID, `none`, or CSS file path |
| `color_scheme` | `auto`, `light`, or `dark` |
| `meta` | Roc record; title and description are statically extracted |

## Markdown profile

Rocdown uses CommonMark with GFM tables, strikethrough, task lists, and extended
URL autolinks. It adds deterministic heading IDs, stable `rd-*` classes,
language classes on fenced code, wiki links, and page-link resolution.

Raw HTML in Markdown is disabled by default. Use Markdown, a document-root
Rocci tag, or `@render` instead.

## Links

Sibling preview supports `[[Page]]`, `[[Page|label]]`, Rocdown file paths, and
same-page heading validation. Absolute routes are checked when a page index is
available. External schemes such as `https:` and `mailto:` pass through.

## Generated values

Every document exports:

```text
rocci_meta    : page metadata record
rocci_content : {} -> Html
rocci_page    : {} -> Html
```

If no GET handler exists for the page route, lowering synthesizes one. A
non-root page also gets a root preview route so `rocci run` can open it.

## Static Rocs support

Rocs currently accepts the static Markdown tree plus `@page`. It rejects Roc,
Rocci, CSS, handlers, and custom layouts until the island splice path is
implemented. Draft pages are excluded from production builds.
